# Craig Transcriber

A Python tool for turning Craig Discord recordings into readable, speaker-labeled transcripts.

This project is built for Discord-based sessions like D&D games. Instead of recording voice directly from Discord, it uses multitrack audio exported from Craig, transcribes each speaker track, and produces a merged transcript with timestamps.

## Features

- Uses Craig multitrack recordings from Discord
- Supports separate speaker audio tracks
- Transcribes speech with the OpenAI API
- Splits tracks into smaller speech chunks
- Produces a timestamped transcript in timeline order

## Project Structure

```text
CraigTranscriber/
├─ .env
├─ .gitignore
├─ requirements.txt
├─ input_zips/
├─ extracted/
├─ outputs/
├─ temp_chunks/
└─ src/
   ├─ main.py
   ├─ config.py
   ├─ extract.py
   ├─ discover.py
   ├─ chunk.py
   ├─ transcribe.py
   └─ merge.py


Setup
Clone the repo
Create and activate a virtual environment
Install dependencies
Add your OpenAI API key to .env


Create virtual environment
py -3 -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

Install dependencies
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt

.env
Create a .env file in the project root:
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here
TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL=gpt-4o-transcribe

How to Use
1. Record a Discord session using Craig
2. Download the multitrack FLAC ZIP from Craig
3. Place the ZIP file into the input_zips/ folder
4. Run the script: python .\src\main.py


Current Status

The core pipeline is working:

ZIP extraction
speaker track discovery
speech chunking
transcription
merged timestamped transcript output

Planned improvements include:

mapping Craig track names to actual Discord usernames
better cleanup of temporary files
D&D-specific summaries and notes generation